---
/* Privacy and cookies. Written from what the site actually does. Controller details come from
 * content/site.json (privacy.controller, privacy.contactEmail); nothing is invented while they are missing. */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import model from '../../lib/content.mjs';
import { longDate } from '../../lib/ui.mjs';
const site = model.site, p = site.privacy || {}, nl = site.newsletter || {};
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy and cookies' }];
const preview = model.target !== 'public';
const missing = (what: string) => preview ? `[${what}: to be supplied]` : null;
---
<Base title="Privacy and cookies | How We Play" description="How How We Play uses Google Analytics (only if you accept), how The Coaching Notes newsletter handles your email, and how to change your choices." ids={['about']} crumbs={crumbs} editorial>
  <div class="page-head ed-grid">
    <div class="page-head__text">
      <p class="ed-kicker">Privacy and cookies</p>
      <h1 class="privacy-h1">Your data, kept to a minimum</h1>
      <p class="ed-stand">How We Play is free to read without giving us anything. This page explains the information you may choose to share when subscribing, getting in touch or accepting analytics.</p>
      <p class="byline">Last updated {longDate(p.lastUpdated)}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="ed-grid about-body">
    <div class="story privacy">
      <h2 class="story__h" id="who">Who runs How We Play</h2>
      <p>How We Play is an independent project written by {site.author.name}. {p.controller ? `The data controller is ${p.controller}.` : (missing('Data controller name and status') || '')}</p>
      <p>For privacy questions or requests, use our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and choose <strong>Privacy enquiry</strong>.</p>

      <h2 class="story__h" id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages and guides are used, so we know what to write next. It only runs if you choose <strong>Accept analytics</strong>. Until then, no analytics code loads and no analytics cookies are set.</p>
      <p>If you accept, Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_…</code>) and records things like the pages you view, roughly where you are (country or city), your device and browser, and a few actions such as following a link to Ko-fi or downloading a playbook. We don't send your name, email address or anything you type. Google signals and advertising features are switched off.</p>
      <p>We keep your choice in your browser's local storage so we don't ask again on every page. That's needed to remember the choice and isn't used for anything else.</p>
      <p><strong>Changing your mind:</strong> use <button type="button" class="inline-btn" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button> (also in the footer of every page). If you switch analytics off, we stop it and remove its cookies.</p>
      <p>Google processes this data for us. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's privacy policy<span class="hwp-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>

      <h2 class="story__h" id="contact">Contact form</h2>
      <p>If you send an enquiry, we collect the name, email address, subject and message that you provide. We use these only to read your enquiry and reply to you, not to subscribe you to The Coaching Notes or send marketing.</p>
      <p>Form messages are processed by Cloudflare Email Service and sent to the project owner's inbox, currently hosted by Google (Gmail). Messages are retained only for as long as reasonably necessary to respond and manage the enquiry. Please avoid including personal details about children or sensitive information.</p>
      <p>We do not use submitted form content as an analytics event or display it publicly. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare's privacy policy<span class="hwp-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's privacy policy<span class="hwp-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>

      <h2 class="story__h" id="newsletter">The Coaching Notes newsletter</h2>
      <p>If you sign up, we collect your email address only, to send you The Coaching Notes: new formation issues, occasional coaching ideas and practical resources. It isn't daily or weekly; we only send something when there's something worth sending.</p>
      <p>Signups are handled by Mailchimp (Intuit), which stores your email and a record of when and how you subscribed.{nl.doubleOptIn ? ' You will get an email asking you to confirm before you are added.' : ''} See <a href="https://www.intuit.com/privacy/statement/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Intuit's privacy statement<span class="hwp-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
      <p>Every email has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing takes effect straight away. We don't share or sell your email, and we don't add anyone to the newsletter because they downloaded a playbook or supported us on Ko-fi.</p>

      <h2 class="story__h" id="kofi">Supporting us on Ko-fi</h2>
      <p>"Support How We Play" and "Buy me a coffee" links go to our page on Ko-fi, a separate website with its own privacy policy. We don't receive your payment details. Supporting us never signs you up to anything.</p>

      <h2 class="story__h" id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to see the personal data we hold about you, to correct it, to delete it, or to object to how it's used. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk<span class="hwp-sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
